cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the accompanying paper, please cite it as below."
title: "The Readout Regime: A Normal Form for Final-Residual Control of Frozen Transformers — and Its Capacity Limits"
abstract: >-
  Companion code and result artifacts for the Readout Regime paper. A
  final-residual additive intervention on a frozen transformer acts on every
  input as a positive scalar temperature plus a re-ranking bias confined to a
  fixed, low-dimensional cone chosen before any input (T1, T2). This repository
  reproduces the empirical map: the closed-form verification, the basis-privilege
  probes, the K-target capacity ceiling, the cross-scale recall, and the Tier-B
  walls.
type: software
authors:
